    "settings": [{"type":"paragraph","content":"Section design by GemPages. [Click here to start design](https://admin.shopify.com/store/429531/apps/gempages-cro/app/shopify/edit?pageType=GP_ARTICLE&editorId=576267057851532227&sectionId=576270161904927570)"},{"type":"select","label":"Section Preload","id":"section_preload","options":[{"label":"On","value":"true"},{"label":"Off","value":"false"},{"label":"Off Lazy Script","value":"off_lazy_script"}],"default":"false"},{"type":"text","label":"Checksum","id":"checksum"},{"type":"html","id":"gg2yBbNwNwT_text","label":"gg2yBbNwNwT_text","default":"<span style=\"font-size:42px;\">FAQs</span>"},{"type":"html","id":"ggfMlFPKF_M_childItem_0","label":"ggfMlFPKF_M_childItem_0","default":"<p>What are the side effects of bakuchiol serum?</p>"},{"type":"html","id":"ggfMlFPKF_M_childItem_1","label":"ggfMlFPKF_M_childItem_1","default":"<p>How does bakuchiol compare to retinol?</p>"},{"type":"html","id":"ggfMlFPKF_M_childItem_2","label":"ggfMlFPKF_M_childItem_2","default":"<p>What makes bakuchiol a popular choice in skincare?</p>"},{"type":"html","id":"ggfMlFPKF_M_childItem_3","label":"ggfMlFPKF_M_childItem_3","default":"<p>Who should consider using bakuchiol serum?</p>"},{"type":"html","id":"ggfMlFPKF_M_childItem_4","label":"ggfMlFPKF_M_childItem_4","default":"<p>Can bakuchiol help with acne?</p>"},{"type":"html","id":"ggfMlFPKF_M_childItem_5","label":"ggfMlFPKF_M_childItem_5","default":"<p>Do I need to patch test bakuchiol before using it?</p>"},{"type":"html","id":"ggfMlFPKF_M_childItem_6","label":"ggfMlFPKF_M_childItem_6","default":"<p>Can bakuchiol be used alongside other skincare ingredients?</p>"},{"type":"html","id":"ggfMlFPKF_M_childItem_7","label":"ggfMlFPKF_M_childItem_7","default":"<p>Is bakuchiol suitable for pregnant or nursing individuals?</p>"},{"type":"html","id":"ggtZ6ubTu5d_text","label":"ggtZ6ubTu5d_text","default":"<p>Bakuchiol serum side effects are usually mild. You might see slight redness, dryness, or irritation. Rarely, people might get itchiness or a mild rash. Always do a patch test before using it to check for sensitivity.</p>"},{"type":"html","id":"ggK4nW1hCUW_text","label":"ggK4nW1hCUW_text","default":"<p>Bakuchiol is like a natural retinol because it fights fine lines and wrinkles. It doesn't dry out or cause redness like retinol can. But, start slow if your skin is sensitive.</p>"},{"type":"html","id":"gg3cMGG9orB_text","label":"gg3cMGG9orB_text","default":"<p>Bakuchiol is from the Babchi plant and is loved for its anti-aging benefits. It brightens the skin and is gentle on sensitive skin. It supports collagen and is less likely to irritate than stronger ingredients.</p>"},{"type":"html","id":"gg2-VmBHBX5_text","label":"gg2-VmBHBX5_text","default":"<p>Anyone who finds retinol too harsh might like bakuchiol. It's good for fine lines, uneven tone, and hyperpigmentation. Young and old can use it for gentle anti-aging.</p>"},{"type":"html","id":"gg2DxIyxcy1_text","label":"gg2DxIyxcy1_text","default":"<p>Yes, bakuchiol can help with mild acne by clearing pores. But, for severe acne, see a dermatologist.</p>"},{"type":"html","id":"gg6L0nIMqHw_text","label":"gg6L0nIMqHw_text","default":"<p>Yes, if your skin is sensitive. Apply a small amount to your forearm or behind your ear. Wait 24 to 48 hours. If no reaction, it's safe for your face.</p>"},{"type":"html","id":"gg7d7WdWyQH_text","label":"gg7d7WdWyQH_text","default":"<p>Usually yes, but be careful not to mix too many strong ingredients. If using AHAs, BHAs, or retinol, use them on different days. Or ask a pro to make sure your routine is balanced.</p>"},{"type":"html","id":"gg6I4Qc93AT_text","label":"gg6I4Qc93AT_text","default":"<p>Some say bakuchiol is safer than retinoids for pregnant or nursing moms. But, no ingredient is completely safe. Always talk to a healthcare provider or dermatologist before using it.</p>"}],
